{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1dd9dc5e-0fb2-4740-9748-52aa3c0f5b94","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b91fe7b92b443226","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-fva3kn_p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E003.md","content":"# Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n\n## Description\n\nAuthors the contribution guideline that specifies the structured log field convention adopted for rhods-operator reconciliation error logs — required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's structured log key conventions), and the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing `resourceKind`) — with before/after code examples and a DSCI key-migration guide, and publishes the convention for voluntary adoption by external operator teams (Cluster Observability Operator components: Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) per platform policy overlay 0008 (RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies).\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline of the guideline and publication deliverables:\n\n- Contribution guideline for new controller development specifying:\n  - the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) and when each applies (including cluster-scoped resources, where `namespace` is omitted or empty);\n  - the camelCase naming rationale, matching controller-runtime's existing structured log key conventions;\n  - the three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and the missing `resourceKind` field;\n  - before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs;\n  - a DSCI key-name migration guide with before/after Loki/CloudWatch query examples suitable for release notes, supporting a single-release transition away from the old field names.\n- Publication of the convention as a specification for voluntary external operator adoption, including filing tracking issues in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects so adoption is discoverable, while acknowledging external adoption is best-effort per platform policy.\n- Technical validation of the guideline against the implemented conversions in the rhods-operator manager and cloudmanager binaries, so the documented examples match shipped behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The structured log field convention is documented in a contribution guideline specifying the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing `resourceKind`).\n- The guideline includes before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs, and a DSCI key-migration guide with before/after query examples that can be reused in release notes.\n- The convention is published as a specification for external operator adoption, and tracking issues are filed in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects.\n- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary log conversions — the reviewer confirms the documented field names, examples, and migration guidance match the shipped behavior.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-8 (P1) — document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70938,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9e94f49b8902cf1","agent_id":"adafcd0706974ac1e","session_id":"93f42fce-654c-40a2-8301-f2dce4eb00ac","uuid":"35eab1cb-d81f-4177-b095-e7468a4e46