{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-954d18a2d0a647ee","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator cloudmanager\n4\t  binary\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator cloudmanager binary\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tApplies the same structured logging convention to the cloudmanager binary shipped with the rhods-operator, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its three reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the same controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern and already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger. This epic converts message-embedded resource identity in error paths to structured key-value pairs, adds the `resourceKind` structured field, and includes authoring and verifying the part of the CI lint/static-analysis enforcement that covers this binary's converted call sites.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Audit `log.Error()` call sites in the reconciliation error paths of the three cloudmanager infrastructure controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine).\n39\t- For each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n40\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all reconciliation error logs in these controllers (kind is not implied by the controller name).\n41\t- Handle cluster-scoped infrastructure resources consistently with the platform convention: emit `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or empty where the resource is cluster-scoped.\n42\t- Author and verify the part of the CI lint rule (or static-analysis check) covering this binary's converted call sites.\n43\t- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Given a cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by a unit test asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output.\n48\t- Given a cloudmanager reconciliation error log that previously embedded resource identity in the message string, when the code is updated, then it uses structured key-value pairs instead — measured by the lint rule / static analysis reporting zero remaining embedded-identity `log.Error` calls in this binary.\n49\t- The lint rule covering this binary's converted call sites runs in CI and fails on `log.Error` calls embedding name/namespace in message text or missing required structured fields.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-1 (P0) — reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`): cloudmanager-binary portion.\n54\t- HLR-5 (P0) — all cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n55\t\n56\t## Notes\n57\t\n58\tRelease timing (same release as the manager-binary work vs. a subsequent release) is an open PM/ODH Operator team scheduling decision; it does not change this epic's scope. The log-consumer regression and alert-rule coordination for the platform is tracked with the manager-binary work; cloudmanager runs only on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave), so its log-consumer surface is narrower.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e3b0b98c623d1ec","agent_id":"a23d7c700483192f4","session_id":"93f42fce-654c-40a2-8301-f2dce4eb00ac","uuid":"fecfddd9-b868-4d3d-bb73-6b7b15b24f95","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:51:42.462Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-954d18a2d0a647ee","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
