{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba5b61444e069653","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator manager binary\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator manager binary\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tConverts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and adds the `resourceKind` structured field across every reconciliation error log path in the manager binary of the rhods-operator: the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller, and the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — plus all 15 action files across 4 tiers: 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`). The epic also migrates the DSCI controller from non-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`). It includes authoring and verifying the part of the CI lint/static-analysis enforcement that covers this binary's converted call sites.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary's five controller tiers and 15 action files (grep/static analysis), producing the call-site checklist that tracks conversion coverage and confirming the assumed ~75% embedded-identity share.\n38\t- For each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n39\t- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured field names from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace` (single-release transition).\n40\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all reconciliation error logs — required for service controllers, the module controller and its handlers, and all action files (kind not implied by controller name), and for the DSC and component controllers as a cross-controller queryability enhancement over the same call sites.\n41\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or empty — never a spurious namespace value.\n42\t- Author and verify the CI lint rule (or static-analysis check) covering this binary's converted call sites, flagging `log.Error` calls that embed name/namespace in message text or omit required structured fields.\n43\t- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via test logger output, per controller tier and across all 15 action files.\n44\t- Backwards-compatibility validation per the strategy NFR: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error; verify a production log consumer (Loki, CloudWatch) ingests both formats without configuration changes on a dev cluster; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify and update any text-based alert rules that rely on message-string patterns before merge.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Given a reconciliation error log call in any manager-binary controller that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the log call uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) instead — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis reporting zero remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text in this binary.\n49\t- Given the DSCI controller's reconciliation error logs, when the code is updated, then all structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) — measured by a unit test asserting DSCI error logs contain the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to the old field names remain.\n50\t- Given a service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `resourceKind` as a structured field with the correct value — measured by a unit test parsing test logger output.\n51\t- Given an action file error log in any of the 4 tiers, when the code is updated, then the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by unit tests asserting all three fields with correct values across all 15 action files.\n52\t- Given the module controller reconciles any of its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator) and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` — measured by a unit test asserting field presence and correctness.\n53\t- Given a cluster-scoped resource (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) is reconciled and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name` and `resourceKind` and `namespace` is omitted or set to empty string — measured by a unit test confirming cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n54\t- The lint rule covering this binary's converted call sites runs in CI and fails on any `log.Error` call embedding name/namespace in message text or missing required structured fields.\n55\t- Before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms the structured fields appear and the production log consumer stack ingests both formats without configuration changes (dev-cluster validation), with text-based alert rules identified and updated in coordination with SRE/Support.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-1 (P0) — all manager-binary reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n60\t- HLR-2 (P0) — DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names to camelCase convention.\n61\t- HLR-3 (P0) — all service controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n62\t- HLR-4 (P0) — all action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (15 files).\n63\t- HLR-6 (P0) — module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers).\n64\t- HLR-7 (P1, bundled) — DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`. Bundled with the P0 conversion: it is the same `log.Error` call sites as HLR-1/HLR-4, so a split would audit and re-review the same files twice; not separately schedulable.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7335c129edb3f57","agent_id":"aa0fa9c21920d82b5","session_id":"93f42fce-654c-40a2-8301-f2dce4eb00ac","uuid":"2b631c3b-